## Implementation Phases

### Phase 1: Foundation (VAD Mode Focus)
**Goal:** Basic web server with job submission and monitoring for VAD-split-audio mode

**Backend Tasks:**
- [ ] Set up FastAPI backend with project structure (`web_api/` directory)
- [ ] Create job model (SQLite: job_id, status, mode, created_at, config_json)
- [ ] Create job submission endpoint (file upload for 2 audio files, configuration)
- [ ] Default mode selection to `vad_split_audio`
- [ ] Integrate with existing `PipelineExecutor` (import, not subprocess)
- [ ] Add progress callback to `VADTranscriptionStage.execute()` method
- [ ] Add per-block callback to `VADASRProcessor.process_blocks()` for granular progress
- [ ] Implement SSE endpoint for job progress events
- [ ] Create checkpoint retrieval endpoint (uses existing `CheckpointLoadResult`)

**Frontend Tasks:**
- [ ] Create React + TypeScript project scaffold
- [ ] Build job configuration form (default to VAD mode, 2-file upload)
- [ ] Build job monitoring view with progress indicators
- [ ] Show per-block transcription progress (VAD specific)
- [ ] Implement SSE client for real-time updates

**Integration Points:**
- Reuse: `PipelineContext`, `PipelineExecutor`, `create_pipeline_for_mode("vad_split_audio")`
- Extend: Add `progress_callback` parameter to stage execution

### Phase 2: Transcript Viewing (Block-Level for VAD)
**Goal:** View and navigate VAD transcripts with audio sync

**Backend Tasks:**
- [ ] Create transcript retrieval endpoint (returns `TranscriptFlow.to_dict()`)
- [ ] Create turns endpoint (returns `HierarchicalTurn` list with interjections)
- [ ] Implement stage-specific output endpoints
- [ ] Add dual audio file serving endpoints (interviewer + participant tracks)
- [ ] Return VAD block info (start_s, end_s, speaker_id, is_interjection)

**Frontend Tasks:**
- [ ] Integrate wavesurfer.js for audio playback
- [ ] Build **dual audio player** - sync two tracks (interviewer + participant)
- [ ] Build transcript display using `HierarchicalTurn` structure
- [ ] Implement **block-level highlighting** (not word-level for VAD mode)
- [ ] Implement speaker color coding
- [ ] Implement block-level click to seek
- [ ] Display interjections visually embedded in primary turns
- [ ] Add timestamp display at turn boundaries
- [ ] Build stage selector dropdown (shows completed stages only)

**Integration Points:**
- Reuse: `TranscriptFlow`, `HierarchicalTurn`, `InterjectionSegment` data structures
- Reuse: `turns-json` writer output format
- Reference: `web_tools/transcript_compare/` for audio sync patterns (adapt, don't copy)

### Phase 3: Basic Editing (Block and Word Level)
**Goal:** Core transcript editing functionality for VAD transcripts

**Backend Tasks:**
- [ ] Design edit storage schema (edits as patches on TranscriptFlow)
  ```sql
  CREATE TABLE edits (
      id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
      job_id TEXT NOT NULL,
      stage_name TEXT NOT NULL,
      edit_type TEXT NOT NULL,  -- block_text_change, word_insert, word_delete, speaker_change
      turn_id INTEGER,          -- Which HierarchicalTurn
      target_index INTEGER,     -- Word index within turn (if applicable)
      original_value TEXT,
      new_value TEXT,
      created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
  );
  ```
- [ ] Implement edit save endpoint
- [ ] Implement "apply edits to TranscriptFlow" logic
- [ ] Add "edited" flag to downstream stages (stale detection)
- [ ] Create endpoint to trigger re-run from checkpoint (uses existing `run_pipeline_from_checkpoint`)

**Frontend Tasks:**
- [ ] Build block selection UI (click to select entire block)
- [ ] Implement click-to-edit block text modal
- [ ] Implement word selection within block
- [ ] Implement insert word (before/after)
- [ ] Implement delete word
- [ ] Build undo/redo system (local state + server sync)
- [ ] Implement auto-save with debounce (2 second delay)
- [ ] Add visual indicators for edited blocks/words
- [ ] Build stale-stage warning UI
- [ ] Build "Re-run Pipeline" confirmation dialog

**Integration Points:**
